<p>To convert <a href="https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/Matroska">Matroska video
files</a> (<code>.mkv</code>), to <a href="https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/WebM">WebM
video files</a> (<code>.webm</code>), I've found
that this command produces good results:</p>
<div class="highlight"><pre><span></span><code>$<span class="w"> </span>ffmpeg<span class="w"> </span>-i<span class="w"> </span>foo.mkv<span class="w"> </span>-c:v<span class="w"> </span>libvpx<span class="w"> </span>-crf<span class="w"> </span><span class="m">10</span><span class="w"> </span>-b:v<span class="w"> </span>1M<span class="w"> </span>-c:a<span class="w"> </span>libvorbis<span class="w"> </span>foo.webm
</code></pre></div>

<p>The resulting <code>foo.webm</code> video file plays natively in Firefox and
Google Chrome, as well as standalone video players like <a href="mpv.io">mpv</a></p>